"type":"text"},{"text":"(AVPlayer: the SDK swaps the ITEM on the same player), and breaks for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"players that rebuild their internal pipeline on a source change: THEOplayer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaces its internal AVPlayer\/layer when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"type":"text","text":" is assigned, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered layer dies, and AVKit closes the window at the exact moment the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SDK lends the content player to the ad. Measured on the iOS e2e fleet"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(catalog-pip, SDK 0.50.0-beta.500): the window opened before the break and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closed at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adbreakbegin"},{"text":", with the ad playing full-screen in the main","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window instead of inside it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Such players expose their own picture-in-picture facility with the missing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"piece — THEOplayer retains the window across source changes when the host","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constructs it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"PiPConfiguration(retainPresentationModeOnSourceChange: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — but only if the window is driven through THAT facility. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol is how an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three members are called on the main thread (the renderer is"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); the change handler must likewise be invoked on the main","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thread, for every transition — including viewer-driven ones (the system UI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can dismiss the window at any time), which is the whole reason the handler","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exists: the break format follows what is actually on screen.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PictureInPictureCapable","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"OptiViewAdsCore"}],"role":"symbol","title":"PictureInPictureCapable","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:15OptiViewAdsCore09PictureInE7CapableP","roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PictureInPictureCapable","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/optiviewadscore\/pictureinpicturecapable"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/isPictureInPicture()","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/onPictureInPictureChange(_:)","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/setPictureInPicture(_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"references":{"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/PlayerAdapter":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlayerAdapter"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter","title":"PlayerAdapter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The abstraction layer between the SDK and any content player — the Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{